dministration\nAdmissions\nCampus Map\nResearch\nFile PBV/Title IX Report\nCrime Stats Report\nGive Today!\nAdmissions\nVisit the Bluff\nApply for Admissions\nEnrollment Steps\nOut of State Fee Waiver\nAdmissions Document Upload\nUndergraduate Admissions Requirements\nInternational Student Admissions Requirements\nInternational Student Visa Requirements\nHonors Admissions\nTransfer Student Admissions\nAdult Student Admissions\nGraduate Student Admissions\nReadmission\nResidency Requirements\nJag Parent Portal\nContact Us\nInquiry Form\nSection Menu\nAdmissions\nVisit the Bluff\nApply for Admissions\nEnrollment Steps\nOut of State Fee Waiver\nAdmissions Document Upload\nUndergraduate Admissions Requirements\nInternational Student Admissions Requirements\nInternational Student Visa Requirements\nHonors Admissions\nTransfer Student Admissions\nAdult Student Admissions\nGraduate Student Admissions\nReadmission\nResidency Requirements\nJag Parent Portal\nContact Us\nInquiry Form\nInternational Student Admissions\nInternational Student Admissions\nInternational Freshmen\nFreshman international students must have completed a recognized secondary program comparable to U.S. high school graduation requirements, and have academic records comparable to those required to meet the freshman admission criteria. Freshman international applicants should meet the following requirements:\nA TOEFL score of 500 (173 on the computer based test) on the paper based test\nAll admitted students must have sufficient knowledge of the English language to benefit from a program of study. All undergraduates whose first language is not English must take the test of English as Foreign Language (TOEFL).\nInternational Transfer Students\nTransfer international students must have completed a recognized secondary program and meet transfer admission criteria. Transfer International applicants should meet the following requirements:\nBe eligible to return to the institution from which s/he is transferring;\nHave earned at least a 2.0 GPA on all college work attempted; and\nHave need for no more than one developmental course. Students in need of more than one developmental course will not be eligible for admission to Southern University.\nAll admitted students must have sufficient knowledge of the English language to benefit from a program of study. All undergraduates whose first language is not English must take the test of English as Foreign Language (TOEFL).\nAll International applicants should meet the following requirements:\nA score of 500 or above on the TOEFL(submit original)\nOfficial High School Transcript\nOfficial /Original West African Examination Scores for students of West Africa\nCurrent NOTARIZED Affidavit of Financial Support (Original)\nCopy of Immunization Form\nCopy of your resident card\nLetter of Good Conduct\n*Note: New Freshman International students from foreign institutions must have high school transcripts evaluated by the World Education Service (WES) or one of the following companies listed before submitting to the Southern University Office of Admissions and Recruitment.\nEvaluation Companies for Foreign Transcripts\nWorld Education Services, Inc.\nPO Box 5087\nBowling Green Station\nNew York, NY 10274\nPhone: 212-966-6311\nFAX: 212-966-6395\nEmail: info@wes.org\nWebsite: http://www.wes.org\nEducational Credential Evaluators, Inc.\nPO Box 92970\nMilwaukee, WI 53202\nPhone: 414-289-3400\nFAX: 414-289-3411\nEmail: eval@ece.org\nWebsite: http://www.ece.org\nInternational Education Research Foundation\nPO Box 3665\nCulver City, CA 90231\nPhone: 310-258-9451\nFAX: 310-342-7086\nEmail: info@ierf.org\nWebsite: http://www.ierf.org\nJosef Silny & Associates, Inc.\nInternational Education Consultants\nPO Box 2488233\nCoral Gables, FL 33124\nPhone: 305-273-1616\nFAX: 305-273-1338\nEmail: info@jsilny.com\nWebsite: http://www.jsilny.com\nNational Association of Credential Services (NACES)\nhttp://www.naces.org\nBureau of Citizenship and Immigration 